1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,382
This is Next Edge, a war room for Pi Next participants.

2
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:10,118
The Pi Next prize pool is two hundred thousand US dollars.

3
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:16,614
But seventy five percent of that goes to engagement and retention, not code.

4
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:22,394
So Next Edge is a tool you come back to, not a report.

5
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:28,862
Start with the topic matcher: five questions about your stack and hours.

6
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:34,714
The engine scores five candidate ideas against your answers.

7
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:41,190
Everything is computed locally, so nothing you answer leaves your device.

8
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:47,494
Then a phased forty six day plan, from eligibility to submission.

9
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:52,906
Every task says why it matters and how long it takes.

10
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:59,726
A daily check-in builds a streak. That is the retention hook.

11
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:05,638
And a research library where every conclusion is cross checked.

12
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:11,730
This is for solo developers and small teams entering Pi Next.

13
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:19,102
Pi is how you sign in. No new account, no email, no password.

14
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:26,114
Your Pi identity is your account. Sign in and progress syncs.

15
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:33,910
Next Edge. Pick the right topic, then finish it. Thank you.
